NAME
       wget - download over HTTP and HTTPS

SYNOPSIS
       wget [options] <url>

DESCRIPTION
       Fetches a URL and saves it, by default under the name taken from
       the URL. TLS 1.3 is supported and certificates are verified
       against the bundle in /etc/ssl/certs.

OPTIONS
       -O F                  write to F (- means standard output)
       -P DIR                save into DIR
       -q, --quiet           no output
       -nv, --no-verbose     less output
       --no-check-certificate  do not verify the server certificate
       -U UA, --user-agent   set the User-Agent
       --header H            add a header (may be repeated)
       --post-data D         POST D
       --post-file F         POST the contents of F
       --user U              basic auth user
       --password P          basic auth password
       --max-redirect N      how many redirects to follow
       --tries N             retry count
       --timeout S           socket timeout

EXAMPLES
       wget https://example.com/file.tar
       wget -O - https://example.com/ | grep title

SEE ALSO
       curl(1), ftp(1), nslookup(1)
